# L §5.5: an ask evaluates every combination of the axes its evaluation reads, and its `for … where` is part of its
# evaluation.  Under mode = a, v[k] = base_v[k] (1, 2), so only k2 passes v[k] > lim (1); under mode = b, alt wins and
# v[k] = 2, 3: both pass.  L §5.18 Lines: one line per binding tuple and distinct result across the axes reached: k1
# is bound under b only; k2 under every option (`*`).  (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.5: axis mode read outside the
# axes the ask reaches.)
=== m.tally
model p8
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = [k1, k2]

axis mode
  a "first reading"
  b "second reading"

input base_v[k in ks]: int
input lim: int

def v[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = base_v[k]
  rule alt beats base = base_v[k] + 1 when mode == b

ask q: k for k in ks where v[k] > lim law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  base_v[k1] = 1
  base_v[k2] = 2
  lim = 1
=== expect
q (k = k1) [mode = b]: k1
  reading: mode = b
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
q (k = k2) [mode = *]: k2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
